on number; fit log-log error curves and report slope per arm.\n- Pre-registered decision rule (stability): \"improvement\" = median error ratio A/B <= 0.5; \"equivalent\" = within [0.5, 2.0] (non-inferiority margin 2x); \"worse\" = > 2.0 or any inf/nan where baselines are finite.\n- FD check: central-difference residual vs analytic/fp64 gradient must show log-log slope in [1.8, 2.2] in h; if not, the FD reference is deemed invalid and fp64-native-autograd is the sole anchor (flagged).\n- Secondary trajectory: compare mean final loss and cross-seed std across arms A/B/C; report effect sizes (Cohen's d on log loss); exploratory, not power-driven.\n- Multiple comparisons: Holm correction across the two time contrasts and the stability contrast.\n\n## 6. Controls and Confound Mitigation\n- Identical model, data, seed, dtype, thread settings across arms; only the differentiation path differs.\n- Randomized arm order per config; single-threaded timing; CPU affinity pinning; thermal break (sleep) between warm and cold config blocks if runtime allows.\n- Memory-reuse isolation: Arm E ablation if available; otherwise Arm C (retain_graph) is the closest counterfactual and the residual confound (other TorchOpt optimizations) is stated as a limitation.\n- Arm D is excluded from timing comparisons so FD cost does not pollute the time analysis.\n- All arms use the same PyTorch version; TorchOpt version pinned and recorded in the report.\n\n## 7. Feasibility Assessment\nRequired environment (sandbox currently lacks all of these; network disabled here):\n- Python 3.10-3.12 (sandbox is 3.14; prefer 3.11 for torch wheel availability), pip with network access.\n- torch==2.x CPU wheel (pinned), torchopt==<latest, pinned at implementation (record exact version), numpy, psutil, scipy, statsmodels (mixed models).\n- CPU: 16 cores assumed; no GPU required.\nEstimated cost:\n- Per MLP config: ~45 x (fwd+bwd) iterations; at dim 2048/batch 1024 on 1 core, ~10-50 ms per iteration -> < 3 s per 